0,Kasa language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kasa_language,"Kasa, or Jóola-Kaasa (also Bacuki, Casa, etc.) is a Jola language of the Casamance region of Senegal and neighboring Gambia. Dialects are Ayun, Bliss (Niomoun), Esulalu (Oussouye), Fluvial, Huluf, Selek.",Jola-Kasa,Niger-Congo
1,Jola languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jola_languages,"Jola (Joola) or Diola is a dialect continuum spoken in Senegal, the Gambia, and Guinea-Bissau. It belongs to the Bak branch of the Niger-Congo language family.",Jola-Kasa,Niger-Congo
